SYNTHETIC – 8.1 entry with the FR-011 masking rules as listed (SecretTextMaskerTest covers
each rule on its own): a stored HTTP message (CRLF)
with Authorization (Basic), Proxy-Authorization (Bearer), X-Api-Key and Cookie lines; a SOAP
body with wsse:Password, a password attribute, a secret-named element with child elements, a
self-closing apiToken element, a token=value query pair, a quoted db_password="…" pair, JSON
string (apiKey) and object (credentials) keys and a Bearer credential in JSON; the configured
password literally in the data, in a variable and in the row's userDefined1; credential-named
variables (apiToken, password:old) and variable values with a secret element and an
Authorization line. Expected: none of the *-secret-0001 values, the Basic credential or the
configured password in the result or the log; placeholders instead; everything else unchanged.

Frames use the fixed nonce 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef; a replay replaces it with the
nonce of its request. Lines without the frame prefix are vendor noise the classifier ignores.
Used by QueueEntryV81ContractTest (tasks.md T026, research D-18, D-19).
